trics/_plot/confusion_matrix.py:ConfusionMatrixDisplay.plot`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `plot`.\nHint: Use more detailed query to get the full content of some if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Based on the search results, the plotting classes in scikit-learn seem to follow a similar pattern, inheriting from a base class and implementing a `plot` method. Let's now get the full content of `DetCurveDisplay`, `PrecisionRecallDisplay`, `RocCurveDisplay`, and `ConfusionMatrixDisplay` to understand their structure and identify the base class they might inherit from.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>\n['sklearn/metrics/_plot/det_curve.py:DetCurveDisplay',\n 'sklearn/metrics/_plot/precision_recall_curve.py:PrecisionRecallDisplay',\n 'sklearn/metrics/_plot/roc_curve.py:RocCurveDisplay',\n 'sklearn/metrics/_plot/confusion_matrix.py:ConfusionMatrixDisplay']\n</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/metrics/_plot/det_curve.py:DetCurveDisplay`...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/metrics/_plot/det_curve.py:DetCurveDisplay`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/metrics/_plot/det_curve.py:DetCurveDisplay`.\n```\n 12 | class DetCurveDisplay:\n 13 |     \"\"\"DET curve visualization.\n 14 | \n 15 |     It is recommend to use :func:`~sklearn.metrics.DetCurveDisplay.from_estimator`\n 16 |     or :func:`~sklearn.metrics.DetCurveDisplay.from_predictions` to create a\n 17 |     visualizer. All parameters are stored as attributes.\n 18 | \n 19 |     Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <visualizations>`.\n 20 | \n 21 |     .. versionadded:: 0.24\n 22 | \n 23 |     Parameters\n 24 |     ----------\n 25 |     fpr : ndarray\n 26 |         False positive rate.\n 27 | \n 28 |     fnr : ndarray\n 29 |         False negative rate.\n 30 | \n 31 |     estimator_name : str, default=None\n 32 |         Name of estimator. If None, the estimator name is not shown.\n 33 | \n 34 |     pos_label : str or int, default=None\n 35 |         The label of the positive class.\n 36 | \n 37 |     Attributes\n 38 |     ----------\n 39 |     line_ : matplotlib Artist\n 40 |         DET Curve.\n 41 | \n 42 |     ax_ : matplotlib Axes\n 43 |         Axes with DET Curve.\n 44 | \n 45 |     figure_ : matplotlib Figure\n 46 |         Figure containing the curve.\n 47 | \n 48 |     See Also\n 49 |     --------\n 50 |     det_curve : Compute error rates for different probability thresholds.\n 51 |     DetCurveDisplay.from_estimator : Plot DET curve given an estimator and\n 52 |         some data.\n 53 |     DetCurveDisplay.from_predictions : Plot DET curve given the true and\n 54 |         predicted labels.\n 55 | \n 56 |     Examples\n 57 |     --------\n 58 |     >>> import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n 59 |     >>> from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n 60 |     >>> from sklearn.metrics import det_curve, DetCurveDisplay\n 61 |     >>> from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n 62 |     >>> from sklearn.svm import SVC\n 63 |     >>> X, y = make_classification(n_samples=1000, random_state=0)\n 64 |     >>> X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n 65 |     ...     X, y, test_size=0.4, random_state=0)\n 66 |     >>> clf = SVC(random_state=0).fit(X_train, y_train)\n 67 |     >>> y_pred = clf.decision_function(X_test)\n 68 |     >>> fpr, fnr, _ = det_curve(y_test, y_pred)\n 69 |     >>> display = DetCurveDisplay(\n 70 |     ...     fpr=fpr, fnr=fnr, estimator_name=\"SVC\"\n 71 |     ... )\n 72 |     >>> display.plot()\n 73 |     <...>\n 74 |     >>> plt.show()\n 75 |     \"\"\"\n 76 | \n 77 |     def __init__(self, *, fpr, fnr, estimator_name=None, pos_label=None):\n 78 |         self.fpr = fpr\n 79 |         self.fnr = fnr\n 80 |         self.estimator_name = estimator_name\n 81 |         self.pos_label = pos_label\n 82 | \n 83 |     @classmethod\n 84 |     def from_estimator(\n 85 |         cls,\n 86 |         estimator,\n 87 |         X,\n 88 |         y,\n 89 |         *,\n 90 |         sample_weight=None,\n 91 |         response_method=\"auto\",\n 92 |         pos_label=None,\n 93 |         name=None,\n 94 |         ax=None,\n 95 |         **kwargs,\n 96 |     ):\n 97 |         \"\"\"Plot DET curve given an estimator and data.\n 98 | \n 99 |         Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <visualizations>`.\n100 | \n101 |         .. versionadded:: 1.0\n102 | \n103 |         Parameters\n104 |         ----------\n105 |         estimator : estimator instance\n106 |             Fitted classifier or a fitted :class:`~sklearn.pipeline.Pipeline`\n107 |             in which the last estimator is a classifier.\n108 | \n109 |         X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n110 |             Input values.\n111 | \n112 |         y : array-like of shape (n_samples,)\n113 |             Target values.\n114 | \n115 |         sample_weight : array-like of shape (n_samples,), default=None\n116 |             Sample weights.\n117 | \n118 |         response_method : {'predict_proba', 'decision_function', 'auto'} \\\n119 |                 default='auto'\n120 |             Specifies whether to use :term:`predict_proba` or\n121 |             :term:`decision_function` as the predicted target response. If set\n122 |             to 'auto', :term:`predict_proba` is tried first and if it does not\n123 |             exist :term:`decision_function` is tried next.\n124 | \n125 |         pos_label : str or int, default=None\n126 |             The label of the positive class. When `pos_label=None`, if `y_true`\n127 |             is in {-1, 1} or {0, 1}, `pos_label` is set to 1, otherwise an\n128 |             error will be raised.\n129 | \n130 |         name : str, default=None\n131 |             Name of DET curve for labeling. If `None`, use the name of the\n132 |             estimator.\n133 | \n134 |         ax : matplotlib axes, default=None\n135 |             Axes object to plot on. If `None`, a new figure and axes is\n136 |             created.\n137 | \n138 |         **kwargs : dict\n139 |             Additional keywords arguments passed to matplotlib `plot` function.\n140 | \n141 |         Returns\n142 |         -------\n143 |         display : :class:`~sklearn.metrics.DetCurveDisplay`\n144 |             Object that stores computed values.\n145 | \n146 |         See Also\n147 |         --------\n148 |         det_curve : Compute error rates for different probability thresholds.\n149 |         DetCurveDisplay.from_predictions : Plot DET curve given the true and\n150 |             predicted labels.\n151 |         plot_roc_curve : Plot Receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve.\n152 | \n153 |         Examples\n154 |         --------\n155 |         >>> import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n156 |         >>> from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n157 |         >>> from sklearn.metrics import DetCurveDisplay\n158 |         >>> from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n159 |         >>> from sklearn.svm import SVC\n160 |         >>> X, y = make_classification(n_samples=1000, random_state=0)\n161 |         >>> X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n162 |         ...     X, y, test_size=0.4, random_state=0)\n163 |         >>> clf = SVC(random_state=0).fit(X_train, y_train)\n164 |         >>> DetCurveDisplay.from_estimator(\n165 |         ...    clf, X_test, y_test)\n166 |         <...>\n167 |         >>> plt.show()\n168 |         \"\"\"\n169 |         check_matplotlib_support(f\"{cls.__name__}.from_estimator\")\n170 | \n171 |         name = estimator.__class__.__name__ if name is None else name\n172 | \n173 |         y_pred, pos_label = _get_response(\n174 |             X,\n175 |             estimator,\n176 |             response_method,\n177 |             pos_label=pos_label,\n178 |         )\n179 | \n180 |         return cls.from_predictions(\n181 |             y_true=y,\n182 |             y_pred=y_pred,\n183 |             sample_weight=sample_weight,\n184 |             name=name,\n185 |             ax=ax,\n186 |             pos_label=pos_label,\n187 |             **kwargs,\n188 |         )\n189 | \n190 |     @classmethod\n191 |     def from_predictions(\n192 |         cls,\n193 |         y_true,\n194 |         y_pred,\n195 |         *,\n196 |         sample_weight=None,\n197 |         pos_label=None,\n198 |         name=None,\n199 |         ax=None,\n200 |         **kwargs,\n201 |     ):\n202 |         \"\"\"Plot DET curve given the true and\n203 |         predicted labels.\n204 | \n205 |         Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <visualizations>`.\n206 | \n207 |         .. versionadded:: 1.0\n208 | \n209 |         Parameters\n210 |         ----------\n211 |         y_true : array-like of shape (n_samples,)\n212 |             True labels.\n213 | \n214 |         y_pred : array-like of shape (n_samples,)\n215 |             Target scores, can either be probability estimates of the positive\n216 |             class, confidence values, or non-thresholded measure of decisions\n217 |             (as returned by `decision_function` on some classifiers).\n218 | \n219 |         sample_weight : array-like of shape (n_samples,), default=None\n220 |             Sample weights.\n221 | \n222 |         pos_label : str or int, default=None\n223 |             The label of the positive class. When `pos_label=None`, if `y_true`\n224 |             is in {-1, 1} or {0, 1}, `pos_label` is set to 1, otherwise an\n225 |             error will be raised.\n226 | \n227 |         name : str, default=None\n228 |             Name of DET curve for labeling. If `None`, name will be set to\n229 |             `\"Classifier\"`.\n230 | \n231 |         ax : matplotlib axes, default=None\n232 |             Axes object to plot on. If `None`, a new figure and axes is\n233 |             created.\n234 | \n235 |         **kwargs : dict\n236 |             Additional keywords arguments passed to matplotlib `plot` function.\n237 | \n238 |         Returns\n239 |         -------\n240 |         display : :class:`~sklearn.metrics.DetCurveDisplay`\n241 |             Object that stores computed values.\n242 | \n243 |         See Also\n244 |         --------\n245 |         det_curve : Compute error rates for different probability thresholds.\n246 |         DetCurveDisplay.from_estimator : Plot DET curve given an estimator and\n247 |             some data.\n248 |         plot_roc_curve : Plot Receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve.\n249 | \n250 |         Examples\n251 |         --------\n252 |         >>> import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n253 |         >>> from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n254 |         >>> from sklearn.metrics import DetCurveDisplay\n255 |         >>> from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n256 |         >>> from sklearn.svm import SVC\n257 |         >>> X, y = make_classification(n_samples=1000, random_state=0)\n258 |         >>> X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n259 |         ...     X, y, test_size=0.4, random_state=0)\n260 |         >>> clf = SVC(random_state=0).fit(X_train, y_train)\n261 |         >>> y_pred = clf.decision_function(X_test)\n262 |         >>> DetCurveDisplay.from_predictions(\n263 |         ...    y_test, y_pred)\n264 |         <...>\n265 |         >>> plt.show()\n266 |         \"\"\"\n267 |         check_matplotlib_support(f\"{cls.__name__}.from_predictions\")\n268 |         fpr, fnr, _ = det_curve(\n269 |             y_true,\n270 |             y_pred,\n271 |             pos_label=pos_label,\n272 |             sample_weight=sample_weight,\n273 |         )\n274 | \n275 |         pos_label = _check_pos_label_consistency(pos_label, y_true)\n276 |         name = \"Classifier\" if name is None else name\n277 | \n278 |         viz = DetCurveDisplay(\n279 |             fpr=fpr,\n280 |             fnr=fnr,\n281 |             estimator_name=name,\n282 |             pos_label=pos_label,\n283 |         )\n284 | \n285 |         return viz.plot(ax=ax, name=name, **kwargs)\n286 | \n287 |     def plot(self, ax=None, *, name=None, **kwargs):\n288 |         \"\"\"Plot visualization.\n289 | \n290 |         Parameters\n291 |         ----------\n292 |         ax : matplotlib axes, default=None\n293 |             Axes object to plot on. If `None`, a new figure and axes is\n294 |             created.\n295 | \n296 |         name : str, default=None\n297 |             Name of DET curve for labeling. If `None`, use the name of the\n298 |             estimator.\n299 | \n300 |         **kwargs : dict\n301 |             Additional keywords arguments passed to matplotlib `plot` function.\n302 | \n303 |         Returns\n304 |         -------\n305 |         display : :class:`~sklearn.metrics.plot.DetCurveDisplay`\n306 |             Object that stores computed values.\n307 |         \"\"\"\n308 |         check_matplotlib_support(\"DetCurveDisplay.plot\")\n309 | \n310 |         name = self.estimator_name if name is None else name\n311 |         line_kwargs = {} if name is None else {\"label\": name}\n312 |         line_kwargs.update(**kwargs)\n313 | \n314 |         import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n315 | \n316 |         if ax is None:\n317 |             _, ax = plt.subplots()\n318 | \n319 |         (self.line_,) = ax.plot(\n320 |             sp.stats.norm.ppf(self.fpr),\n321 |             sp.stats.norm.ppf(self.fnr),\n322 |             **line_kwargs,\n323 |         )\n324 |         info_pos_label = (\n325 |             f\" (Positive label: {self.pos_label})\" if self.pos_label is not None else \"\"\n326 |         )\n327 | \n328 |         xlabel = \"False Positive Rate\" + info_pos_label\n329 |         ylabel = \"False Negative Rate\" + info_pos_label\n330 |         ax.set(xlabel=xlabel, ylabel=ylabel)\n331 | \n332 |         if \"label\" in line_kwargs:\n333 |             ax.legend(loc=\"lower right\