update_class_log_prior`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n525 | def _update_class_log_prior(self, class_prior=None):\n526 |         n_classes = len(self.classes_)\n527 |         if class_prior is not None:\n528 |             if len(class_prior) != n_classes:\n529 |                 raise ValueError(\"Number of priors must match number of classes.\")\n530 |             self.class_log_prior_ = np.log(class_prior)\n531 |         elif self.fit_prior:\n532 |             with warnings.catch_warnings():\n533 |                 # silence the warning when count is 0 because class was not yet\n534 |                 # observed\n535 |                 warnings.simplefilter(\"ignore\", RuntimeWarning)\n536 |                 log_class_count = np.log(self.class_count_)\n537 | \n538 |             # empirical prior, with sample_weight taken into account\n539 |             self.class_log_prior_ = log_class_count - np.log(self.class_count_.sum())\n540 |         else:\n541 |             self.class_log_prior_ = np.full(n_classes, -np.log(n_classes))\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/discriminant_analysis.py:_class_means`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 96 | def _class_means(X, y):\n 97 |     \"\"\"Compute class means.\n 98 | \n 99 |     Parameters\n100 |     ----------\n101 |     X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n102 |         Input data.\n103 | \n104 |     y : array-like of shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_targets)\n105 |         Target values.\n106 | \n107 |     Returns\n108 |     -------\n109 |     means : array-like of shape (n_classes, n_features)\n110 |         Class means.\n111 |     \"\"\"\n112 |     classes, y = np.unique(y, return_inverse=True)\n113 |     cnt = np.bincount(y)\n114 |     means = np.zeros(shape=(len(classes), X.shape[1]))\n115 |     np.add.at(means, y, X)\n116 |     means /= cnt[:, None]\n117 |     return means\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/discriminant_analysis.py:_class_cov`.\nSource: Re